      "writtenOn": "2024-05-14T23:29:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good catch, but I wonder what a reasonable upper bound for a number of waiting tasks are? Assuming that each task has a runnable_avg of 1024, we\u0027d have a maximum limit of (2^32-1)/1024 \u003d 4194303 tasks or alternatively we can reduce util_avg to 16bits and have 48 bits to work with (2^48-1)/1024 \u003d 274877906943. Those seem like large enough of a margin for the system to work with, thoughts?",
